summary is: {{ CHIEF COMPLAINT

Left elbow pain.

HISTORY OF PRESENT ILLNESS

Ms. Anna Smith is a 26-year-old female with a past medical history significant for epilepsy, depression, and peptic ulcer disease, who presents with left elbow pain.

Ms. Smith reports that her left elbow has been stiff and painful for the past few weeks. She works at a desk and spends most of her day typing. She denies any numbness or tingling in her hands. She has no weakness in her arm. She denies any fever or chills. She is right handed. She has been taking Keppra 500 mg twice daily for the past year. She is in therapy for her depression. She denies any suicidal or homicidal ideations.

Ms. Smith reports that she has been having nasal congestion due to allergies.

Ms. Smith had an esophagogastroduodenoscopy in the past year for peptic ulcer disease. She is doing well with this.

REVIEW OF SYSTEMS

• Constitutional: Denies fevers or chills.
• Musculoskeletal: Reports left elbow pain, stiffness, and swelling.
• Neurological: Denies weakness, numbness, or tingling.
• Respiratory: Endorses nasal congestion.

PHYSICAL EXAM

• Neck: Supple without midline tenderness.
• Respiratory: Lungs are clear to auscultation. No wheezes, rales, or rhonchi.
• Cardiovascular: Regular rate and rhythm. No murmurs, gallops, or rubs. No extra heart sounds.
• Musculoskeletal: Left elbow shows erythema and edema. Pain to palpation of the olecranon. Warm to palpation. Pain with flexion and extension of the left elbow. Palpable right radial pulse.

RESULTS

Left elbow X-ray: No evidence of any elbow fracture.

Esophagogastroduodenoscopy: Revealed gastritis.

ASSESSMENT AND PLAN

Ms. Anna Smith is a 26-year-old female with a past medical history significant for epilepsy, depression, and peptic ulcer disease, who presents with left elbow pain.

Epilepsy.
• Medical Reasoning: The patient is doing well with her Keppra 500 mg twice daily.
• Medical Treatment: Continue Keppra 500 mg twice daily. Obtain a refill.

Depression.
• Medical Reasoning: She is doing well with therapy.
• Medical Treatment: We will start her on Lexapro 10 mg once daily. She will follow up in 2 weeks.

Peptic Ulcer Disease.
• Medical Reasoning: She had an esophagogastroduodenoscopy in the past year for peptic ulcer disease. Her last one resolved after taking Protonix.
• Medical Treatment: Continue Protonix 40 mg once daily prior to meals.

Left Elbow Pain.
• Medical Reasoning: She has repetitive trauma to her left elbow from typing at work.
• Medical Treatment: Continue meloxicam 15 mg once daily. Ice the area.

Patient Agreements: The patient understands and agrees with the recommended medical treatment plan.

INSTRUCTIONS

The patient will follow up in 2 weeks. }}<|eot_id|>
