High blood pressure.

HISTORY OF PRESENT ILLNESS

Susan Johnson is a 26-year-old female who presents for a blood pressure check. The patient reports that she has always struggled with high blood pressure, but it has been getting out of control lately. She wants to see if there is a new medication she can be on to help get her blood pressure under control or if there are any dietary restrictions she should take. She has been on Norvasc, which we had to increase the dose to 10 mg daily. She has had some headaches, but denies chest pain, shortness of breath, etc.

SURGICAL HISTORY

