SOCIAL HISTORY

She is on immunosuppression medications.

MEDICATIONS

She is on Norvasc 10 mg daily.

VITALS

Her blood pressure is high. On physical examination, she is a nontoxic appearing woman in no apparent distress. Her neck is supple. Her heart has an irregular rate and rhythm, and she has a slight 2/6 systolic ejection murmur. Her lungs are clear. She has a healed left flank scar from her kidney transplant and has no lower extremity edema.

RESULTS

Her creatinine is within normal limits. Her EKG is normal.

ASSESSMENT AND PLAN

Susan Johnson is a 26-year-old female who presents for blood pressure check. Her blood pressure is high and the Norvasc is not controlling it. Medical Reasoning: Her creatinine is within normal limits after a kidney transplant a few years ago. Physical examination reveals a supple neck, irregular rate and rhythm, and a slight 2/6 systolic ejection murmur. Her lungs are clear, she has a healed left flank scar from her kidney transplant, and she has no lower extremity edema. Medical Treatment: I am going to prescribe Coreg 25 mg twice daily. I would also like to order a lipid panel and routine labs. She will continue on all of her immunosuppression medications. Patient Agreements: The patient understands and agrees with the recommended medical treatment plan.

Patient Agreements: The patient understands and agrees with the recommended medical treatment plan.

INSTRUCTIONS

Schedule a follow-up appointment in a couple weeks to check blood pressure. }}<|eot_id|>
