summary is: {{ CHIEF COMPLAINT

Full spectrum std testing.

HISTORY OF PRESENT ILLNESS

Ms. Ross is a 23-year-old female who presents today for full spectrum std testing. The patient states that she is having symptoms of discomfort, a change in discharge, and odor in her vaginal region. She states that the right side of her vagina is starting to become painful. She denies any fevers or chills. She reports, that she recently learned, her partner has been in sexual encounters with other people, and she wants to be evaluated for all stds.

The patient states that she has been dating her partner for 3 years and that she believes he has been cheating on her for the past 3 months.

She denies any history of irregular pap smears.

Ms. Ross states that she has noticed a change in the color and consistency of her discharge. She also reports that the discharge smells different. She denies that this initially bothered her until she noticed that the right side of her vagina was hurting. She states that the pain has not gone away.

REVIEW OF SYSTEMS

Constitutional: Denies fevers or chills.
Gastrointestinal: Denies any issues.
Genitourinary: Reports vaginal discharge and pain.
Skin: Denies any rashes.

PHYSICAL EXAM

Genitourinary: Examination of the external genitalia reveals no external lesions. Normal labia majora and labia minora. Normal physiological discharge with normal color and smell. Cervix is normal. Vaginal wall is normal. No cervical motion tenderness and no adnexal tenderness or masses noted.

RESULTS

Swabs were obtained for std testing.

ASSESSMENT AND PLAN

Ms. Ross is a 23-year-old female who presents today for full spectrum std testing. The patient is here after learning that her partner has been in sexual encounters with other people. She has a history of abnormal pap smear. She is concerned that she may have contracted an std.

The patient reports a change in vaginal discharge, pain on the right side of her vagina, and a change in the color of the discharge. She also reports that the discharge smells different. She denies that this initially bothered her until she noticed that the right side of her vagina was hurting. She states that the pain has not gone away.

Her exam is normal. She will be sent for std testing for gonorrhea, chlamydia, trichomoniasis, and blood work for syphilis, hiv, and hepatitis c.

Patient Agreements: The patient understands and agrees with the recommended medical treatment plan.

INSTRUCTIONS

If the patient has not heard from the office in 3 days, she can call to follow up on her results. }}<|eot_id|>
