Mr. Smith has been experiencing intermittent knee pain for quite some time now. He denies any swelling. He denies any recent travel history.

Mr. Smith is on metformin 500 mg twice daily for his diabetes. He is also on Norvasc for his hypertension. He has a dexcom device that monitors his blood sugar levels. He reports that his blood sugar levels spike after meals, up to 200. He denies any low blood sugars. He states that his blood pressure has been running somewhat low, but he does not always take his medications.

