Mr. Dennis Smith is a 57-year-old male who presents today with a chief complaint of shortness of breath. He has a history of diabetes, hypertension, and asthma.

Shortness of breath.
- Medical Reasoning: He has been experiencing shortness of breath for the past couple of weeks. He also reports coughing up blood. His oxygen level in the office today was 94% on pulse oximetry. On physical exam, he has rhonchi and diminished breath sounds on the right side.
