The patient has a history of hypertension, which is controlled with lisinopril 10 mg daily. She reports that her blood pressures have been in the 130s-140s over the past few months. She states that she is compliant with her medications and has an alarm to remind her to take them. She also has a history of diabetes mellitus, which is controlled with metformin 500 mg twice daily. She admits to having a sweet tooth and has been consuming higher amounts of sugar lately. She also enjoys baking and making cakes and scones. She has been doing this since she was young. The patient states that she has had a diabetic consult in the past and is interested in speaking with a dietitian again.

